  "conclusions": {
    "ST-C1": {
      "classification": "APPROVED \u2014 FIXED AND VERIFIED for the scoped failed-legacy-migration backup-exclusion defect",
      "independent_reasoning": [
        "Production iOS DI binds this filesystem into singleton FileBackedSnapshotStore; Home listUnfinished and direct load/loadMetadata reach the modified operations.",
        "Legacy directory exclusion is attempted before list/migrate iteration and before direct-read current-record selection. Thus malformed legacy framing and malformed current framing cannot bypass the exclusion boundary.",
        "Initial directory-protection failure propagates outside corrupt-record migration isolation. Direct reads also propagate; common store maps non-secret snapshot_io rather than hiding failure as empty storage.",
        "Setter and fresh NSURL NSNumber readback must both report success; missing key/path, set failure, readback error or false readback throws.",
        "No corrupt-state normalization, stale-legacy fallback, new data deletion, changed format/key derivation or peer serialization is introduced. Existing recognized-magic failure cleanup remains unchanged and is exercised by two pre-existing safety tests.",
        "Malformed/oversized legacy bytes remain identical and recoverable. Explicit deletion still addresses both copies. Retry re-applies exclusion rather than trusting instance-cached state.",
        "Original actual K/N witness XML contains two passing current-behavior witnesses and one expected failed safety assertion; this is original defect evidence, not a passing repair claim.",
        "Native02 executes eight new production-bound Foundation tests plus six pre-existing storage tests with no failures/skips; changed source hashes match execution before and after."
      ],
      "limitations": [
        "No real iCloud/device backup, restore, prior-backup purge, or incidence among real released users was tested.",
        "Apple explicitly calls isExcludedFromBackup guidance, not a guarantee that an item can never appear in a backup/restored device. Current flag verification is not an end-to-end privacy guarantee.",
        "Focused tests do not execute successful legacy encryption with a real entitlement-bearing Keychain, power-loss/atomic-replacement interruptions, or every mixed healthy/corrupt inventory scenario. Crypto/key APIs and write-before-delete sequencing are unchanged and source-reviewed.",
        "Some native storage tests reuse the suite-level legacy directory; direct-read coverage is therefore combined with explicit injected-call/propagation tests and complete source proof, not represented as independent initial-false filesystem setups for every case.",
        "Production native exception hypothesis/IOS-R1 is not resolved by these tests."
      ]
    },
    "DS-C01": {
      "classification": "APPROVED AS PARTIAL REMEDIATION \u2014 PARTIALLY VERIFIED; legacy unmarked provenance remains unresolved",
      "independent_reasoning": [
        "Reads of prior platform preference and ownership come from the exact application persistent domain, not resolved arrayForKey global/registration fallback.",
        "Marker-before-install records only actual persistent previous data. release validates version, installed String, absence or all-String previous List, and exact current singleton equality before restoring/removing the language key.",
        "Different complete arrays supplied externally survive. Identical unmarked existing values are neither claimed nor removed; malformed prior metadata cannot be installed as AppleLanguages.",
        "apply first reconciles an owned previous lifetime, including a newly constructed owner. System/null still releases; repeated English/Arabic toggles preserve original app-domain absence or actual OS-managed array.",
        "Composition keeps one remembered owner and existing content. No key(language), navigator recreation, game/session recreation, replacement native controller or second navigation system is added. Existing Compose/UIKit direction bridge remains unchanged.",
        "Eleven tests execute the actual Kotlin/Native owner against Foundation UUID suites and restore their domains. They verify synchronous process-visible ownership reconciliation, not a real killed/restarted process.",
        "Native01 two expected-ar fixture assertions failed because global preference wins before registration fallback. Native02 captures the real pre-operation fallback, still asserts persistent-domain absence and restored fallback, and does not alter either production file hash. Correcting that assumption does not weaken the ownership invariant."
      ],
      "limitations": [
        "Legacy unmarked Parlor AppleLanguages is indistinguishable from a legitimate OS per-app value. The fix deliberately preserves it; the original upgrade manifestation can therefore persist and cannot be marked universally fixed.",
        "An external writer setting the exact installed singleton cannot be distinguished from unchanged ownership by value comparison alone.",
        "NSUserDefaults asynchronous persistence and two-key writes are not a power-loss durable transaction. No fresh-process persisted-marker repair execution is claimed.",
        "No actual Compose resource/live UIKit direction/gesture/app-session continuity/restart matrix was run in this focused native suite; source-level retained-composition proof is narrower than UI runtime verification.",
        "Tests ran on owned iOS26.5 simulator with installed Xcode26.5/17F42, not release-qualified26.3/17C529 or physical devices."
      ]
    }
  },
